# Signing / secrets
#
# These are PATTERNS, not exact names, on purpose: the rules used to name
# `telecampro-upload-passwords.txt.gpg` literally, so every ordinary variant escaped them — a
# `.2026-07-07.bak` copy of that very file showed up as committable during the 2026-08-02 keystore
# recovery. A secret that leaks because it was renamed is still a leaked secret.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.gpg
*.asc
*.p12
*.pem
*.pfx
keystore.properties*
!keystore.properties.example
# Extension patterns alone are not enough: a `*.gpg.2026-07-07.bak` copy ends in `.bak`, so it
# matched none of them. Match on the NAME too, and on the archive suffixes people reach for when
# they set a secret aside "for a moment".
*password*
*secret*
*credential*
telecampro-upload-*
*.bak
*.orig

# OS
.DS_Store

